'''Tompkinsville''' is a [[List of Staten Island neighborhoods|neighborhood]] in northeastern [[Staten Island]] in [[New York City]]. Named for [[Daniel D. Tompkins]], sixth [[Vice President of the United States]] (1817–1825), the neighborhood sits on the island's eastern shore, along the waterfront facing [[Upper New York Bay]], between [[St. George, Staten Island|St. George]] on the north and [[Stapleton, Staten Island|Stapleton]] on the south; however, it is considered part of the [[North Shore, Staten Island|North Shore]] by the island's residents.{{citation needed|date=March 2022}}
